{"slug":"hamilton-fish-iv","qid":"Q5644938","name":"Hamilton Fish IV","desc":"American politician (1926–1996)","article":"Hamilton Fish IV","born":"1926-06-03","died":"1996-07-23","birthplace":"Washington, D.C.","parties":["Republican Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NY-19","f":1993,"u":1995},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NY-21","f":1983,"u":1993},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NY-25","f":1973,"u":1983},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NY-28","f":1969,"u":1973}],"summary":"Hamilton Fish IV or Hamilton Fish Jr. (June 3, 1926 – July 23, 1996) was an American Republican politician who represented parts of New York's Hudson Valley region in the United States House of Representatives for thirteen terms from 1969 to 1995. Fish was a member of the prominent Fish political family; his grandfather (Hamilton Fish II) and father (Hamilton Fish III), both also named Hamilton, represented the region from 1909 to 1911 and 1920 to 1945, respectively.","photo":null,"history":[{"y":1992,"o":"H","k":"NY-19","p":"R","v":139610,"s":60.06,"w":true,"n":"Hamilton Fish Jr."},{"y":1990,"o":"H","k":"NY-21","p":"R","v":99866,"s":64.97,"w":true,"n":"Hamilton Fish Jr."},{"y":1988,"o":"H","k":"NY-21","p":"R","v":150443,"s":74.62,"w":true,"n":"Hamilton Fish Jr."},{"y":1986,"o":"H","k":"NY-21","p":"R","v":102070,"s":76.52,"w":true,"n":"Hamilton Fish Jr."},{"y":1984,"o":"H","k":"NY-21","p":"R","v":160053,"s":78.33,"w":true,"n":"Hamilton Fish Jr."},{"y":1982,"o":"H","k":"NY-21","p":"R","v":117460,"s":75.24,"w":true,"n":"Hamilton Fish Jr."},{"y":1980,"o":"H","k":"NY-25","p":"R","v":158936,"s":80.96,"w":true,"n":"Hamilton Fish Jr."},{"y":1978,"o":"H","k":"NY-25","p":"R","v":114641,"s":78.24,"w":true,"n":"Hamilton Fish Jr."},{"y":1976,"o":"H","k":"NY-25","p":"R","v":139389,"s":70.54,"w":true,"n":"Hamilton Fish Jr."}]}